>>>markdown
# Hacker News — a guided tour

A curated slice of the public Hacker News dataset, modeled in Malloy. Two
sources — `stories` (submissions) and `comments` (joined to the story at the root
of each thread) — with reusable, documented measures and chart-tagged views. Open
[`hn.malloy`](hn.malloy) to see how they're defined.

Times are UTC; scores are point-in-time snapshots.
>>>malloy
import "hn.malloy"
>>>markdown
## Overview

One `# dashboard` view, one query: KPI tiles plus the monthly trend, top domains,
category mix, and volume by hour.
>>>malloy
run: stories -> hn_overview
>>>markdown
## Which domains do well?

Average score by domain, for domains with at least 20 stories.
>>>malloy
run: stories -> top_domains
>>>markdown
## When should you post?

Story volume and average score by hour of day (UTC). The two tell different
stories — the busiest hours aren't the highest-scoring ones.
>>>malloy
run: stories -> score_by_hour
>>>markdown
## Ask HN vs Show HN over time

Monthly volume, one line per category.
>>>malloy
run: stories -> ask_vs_show_over_time
>>>markdown
## How rare is a hit?

The distribution of story scores across buckets — most stories never take off.
>>>malloy
run: stories -> score_distribution
>>>markdown
## The most-discussed stories
>>>malloy
run: stories -> most_discussed
>>>markdown
## Crossing the join: comments by the story they're on

`comments` joins to `stories` via each comment's resolved root story, so we can
group comment activity by the category of the story being discussed.
>>>malloy
run: comments -> avg_length_by_category
>>>markdown
## Who comments the most?
>>>malloy
run: comments -> top_commenters
